.TH MATHAUDIODEMO 1
.SH NAME
mathaudiodemo \- the waveform library, plotted
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/mathaudiodemo
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I MathAudioDemo
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/MathAudioDemo.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Three pages, each a trigonometric function in red with its two cheap
audio stand-ins over it in blue and green: sine against the sawtooths,
cosine against the cawtooths, sine against the triangles.  The kernel's
own comments say what the pairs are for \- a sawtooth is "think
(Sin+1)/2" \- and seeing them on the same axes is the demo: how far a
sawtooth is from a sine, and how little that matters at audio rates.
.PP
The functions are transcribed from the kernel, including the sign split
for a negative argument.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "any key"
Add the next curve, or turn the page; the last exits
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/mathaudiodemo.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
